    "values": [
      [
        "Data Quality Issues in MassDOT Crash Reports: Boston, Brookline, Cambridge, Somerville, 2020-2025"
      ],
      [
        "last updated by Jack Dougherty, 2 March 2026"
      ],
      [],
      [
        "Question: MassDOT crash data from state and local police reports is our most reliable source, but what are the quality issues?"
      ],
      [
        "Based on conversation with MassDOT highway safety manager, some quality issues with crash data are due to these factors:"
      ],
      [
        "1) State Police do not successfully geocode many crashes they report, such as missing about 25% somewhere in Boston in 2024"
      ],
      [
        "2) Boston Police did not succesfully report many crashes prior to switching to new MDOT-provided system in 2022"
      ],
      [
        "3) Boston Police did not uniformly code Most Severe Injury prior to switching to new MDOT-provided system in 2022"
      ],
      [
        "4) Some police appear to have mistakenly recorded \"witnesses to a crash\" in the \"Vulnerable Users\" field"
      ],
      [
        "There may be other data quality issues not shown here, including those more directly related to 2020 Covid pandemic"
      ],
      [],
      [
        "Separately, I am still looking into why significant percentages of public crash data from local govts do not seem to appear in MDOT data."
      ],
      [
        "  Local Govt public crash data sources include: Boston Vision Zero (EMS data, not Boston PD data); Cambridge PD; Somerville PD"
      ],
